  "recommendedVerification": [
    "Preserve all original journal and numeric gates, raw data, old failures, begin/end and the 50000us edge rule.",
    "For the new fixture schedule exactly one requested 0ms timeout after the original begin; record actual request, callback entry/exit and scheduling delay separately.",
    "Require a unique owned matching Install and completed Fire with the actual JS timer handle; wrong owner or owned-frame identity mismatch cannot be filtered into a success.",
    "Do not borrow a foreign frame event that happens to reuse the same timer ID; timer ID alone is not a global identifier.",
    "Require both bootstrap marks to have same owned pid/tid and current loader navigationId, physical callTime inside the matching completed Fire, Fire inside an unchanged accepted complete native RunTask and closed measurement window.",
    "The Install data has no navigationId. Establish navigation with before/after document loader identities and Window mark navigation metadata.",
    "Reject missing, multiple, wrong-category, malformed, nonfinite, early/late/unfinished evidence. A timer observed later than 50ms from the unchanged begin remains rejected.",
    "Use separate auxiliary mark names outside the rlab-v3.observe prefix, so the fixed proof validator is not made to accept unknown proof marks.",
    "A successful bootstrap only demonstrates a real post-begin task and the existing edge coverage gate; it cannot recover unrecorded resume-task CPU or prove there are no missing tasks throughout the window."
